                                      same order, and the same two object
                                      codes, sendQuery3Response() already
                                      writes with putIoVector() and
                                      putOutBindValues() (#9984)
    9984-dev-oci23api7-native-inout-realserver.oraproxy
                                     the same, for "begin :v := :v * 2; end;"
                                      with an initial value of 21. the io
                                      vector's direction byte is 0x30 rather
                                      than 0x10, and the server stops there:
                                      the client answers with a TTC_ROW_DATA
                                      packet carrying the in value (02 c1 16,
                                      the number 21, no indicator), and only
                                      then does the server send the out value
                                      (02 c1 2b, 42) and the trailer. so an
                                      in-out bind is a second round trip the
                                      io vector asks for, which is why the
                                      request carries no value (#9984)
    9984-dev-oci23api7-native-nullout-realserver.oraproxy
                                     the same, for "begin :v := NULL; end;".
                                      structurally identical to the out
                                      capture - one packet, same object
                                      order, direction byte 0x10 - with the
                                      value's length byte 0 and the indicator
                                      ff ff (-1, native sb2) where the
                                      non-null capture has 02 c1 08 and
                                      00 00. a null out bind is the same
                                      shape with an empty value and a
                                      negative indicator, not a different
                                      one (#9984)
