    10544-centos6x64-oci11-portable-loginretry-unknownuser-realserver-oracle102.oraproxy
                                     the same 11.2 client against the real
                                      10.2 server (oracle102, 10.0.2.3).
                                      oracle102 is a 32 bit server, so a 64
                                      bit client does not get the 64 bit
                                      native struct from it. The ORA-01017 at
                                      [0019] is a 65 byte object behind the
                                      0x04: ORA number at offset 10, call
                                      number 3 at 44, no 36 01 marker, no
                                      pointer and no second ORA number. The
                                      module classifies the session as
                                      portable, because a 64 bit client sends
                                      the full data type negotiation and the
                                      login request starts with 0x01, but the
                                      fields are fixed width little endian, as
                                      a real server sends them with no
                                      ORAPROXY_UNIVERSAL_REPS, not the count
                                      prefixed form the module sends a
                                      portable session, so this is not a byte
                                      for byte reference for the module. A
                                      native 10.2 object needs a 32 bit client
                                      (redhat9x86) (#10544)

