                                      a later bind request and gets
                                      ORA-03137.  So the integers are in
                                      OCI's native fixed width form,
                                      scale included (b4 01 00 09 28 00
                                      00 00 ...).  Both sides set
                                      RCAP_TTC bit 0x02, the client sends
                                      time zone file version 26 at [0011]
                                      (... 1a d0 07) and the server
                                      answers 26 at [0012], and every
                                      bind at [0017] to [0041] and every
                                      row and out bind is in the UTC
                                      form, the same bytes as the 10.2
                                      capture.  [0075] to [0078] are the
                                      pl/sql out number without and with
                                      an indicator (natively two bytes,
                                      00 00), and [0083] and [0084] the
                                      null (ORA-01405) (#10562)

